note step-unlink <name> <index>: remove the link from one step, so the step reads as a plain step again. The agent reaches for it to undo a wrong link (design.md section 12). Unlike step-link with an empty target, it refuses a step that has no link, so a wrong index shows up as an error instead of silently changing nothing.

